  "step_3": "The decision reason relies on identifying outcomes with probability >50% and averaging those, which in this case leads to indifference (both have only 0€ as a 'probable' outcome). However, the individual did not categorize outcomes based on a 50% threshold, nor did they compute an average of such outcomes. Instead, they compared the prize amounts under the assumption of similar probabilities. The information used by the individual (prize size under near-equal probabilities) differs from the information required by the decision reason (probable outcomes above 50%). Furthermore, the justification—preferring a higher payoff under similar odds—does not align with the rule of averaging probable outcomes. There is no indication that the individual applied the 50% threshold or used it in their reasoning. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
